<title>USA: U.S. Farm Credit to offer two issues of bonds.</title>
<headline>U.S. Farm Credit to offer two issues of bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Farm Credit Bank Funding Corp said Friday it will offer two issues of Federal Farm Credit Banks Consolidated Systemwide Bonds totaling $2.005 billion. The issues will be dated and delivered November 1, 1996.</p>
<p>The first issue is for $1.590 billion and matures on February 3, 1997. It carries a concession of $0.20 per $1,000.</p>
<p>The second issue is for $415 million and matures on May 1, 1997. It carries a concession of $0.30 per $1,000.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
